## Model card

- **Name:** DeepSeek V4.1 Flash
- **Short description:** DeepSeek’s V4.1 Flash (served as `deepseek-flash` per API docs) is positioned as a fast multimodal model for long-context agentic workloads, with very large context/output limits and vision support.
- **Provider / access:** DeepSeek API (`deepseek-flash`) per DeepSeek API docs. Local metadata lists `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash` and `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** API docs list model version `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017`; release/knowledge cutoff details not clearly extracted in this pass.
- **IDs:** `deepseek-flash` (current API name per docs; legacy names noted as routed to V4.1 Flash in docs).
- **Context window:** 1M context length; max output up to 384K (DeepSeek API pricing/model details page).
- **Modalities:** Vision supported for `deepseek-flash` per API model details; text input/output supported (thinking/non-thinking modes, tool calls, JSON output, etc.). Local metadata states text, image in; text out.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** `deepseek-flash` listed at $0.003/$0.006 per 1M input cache-hit (off-peak/peak), $0.15/$0.30 per 1M input cache-miss (off-peak/peak), $0.60/$1.20 per 1M output (off-peak/peak), concurrency limit 2500 (DeepSeek API pricing docs).
- **Architecture:** Local metadata describes 552B multimodal MoE (MIT); architecture details not independently verified from reviewed API docs in this pass.

